Scenario: missionToStr | Verifies that a mission is formatted as a string.
GIVEN a mission with ID 1, facility ID 2, and title "MissionTitle".
WHEN missionToStr is called.
THEN the returned string contains the mission ID, facility ID, and title in the expected format.

Scenario: facilityToStr | Verifies that a facility is formatted as a string.
GIVEN a facility with ID 1, name "FacilityName", and abbreviation "FT".
WHEN facilityToStr is called.
THEN the returned string contains the facility ID, name, and abbreviation in the expected format.

Scenario: briefToStr | Verifies that a brief is formatted as a string.
GIVEN a brief with ID 1, mission ID 2, title "BriefTitle", date "1999-02-15", and content "Content".
WHEN briefToStr is called.
THEN the returned string contains the brief details in the expected format.

Scenario: agentToStr | Verifies that an agent is formatted as a string when the date of death is null.
GIVEN an agent with ID 1, facility ID 3, name "AgentName", date of birth "1999-02-23", a null date of death, and notes "notes".
WHEN agentToStr is called.
THEN the returned string contains the agent details, including a blank date-of-death field and the mission ID shown in the expected format.

Scenario: userToStr | Verifies that a user is formatted as a string.
GIVEN a user with ID 1 and username "userName".
WHEN userToStr is called.
THEN the returned string contains the user ID and username in the expected format.

Scenario: logToStr | Verifies that a logged action is formatted as a string.
GIVEN a logged action with action ID 1, user "userName" with ID 1, date "1999-02-23", and record "record".
WHEN logToStr is called.
THEN the returned string contains the action ID, username, user ID, date, and record in the expected format.

Scenario: messageToStr | Verifies that a message is formatted as a string.
GIVEN a message addressed to agent ID 1 with name "AgentName" and content "Message".
WHEN messageToStr is called.
THEN the returned string contains the recipient agent ID, recipient name, and message content in the expected format.

Scenario: missionsToStr | Verifies that a list of missions is formatted as a list of strings.
GIVEN two missions with different IDs, titles, and facility IDs.
WHEN missionsToStr is called.
THEN the returned list contains the formatted string for each mission in the original order.

Scenario: facilitiesToStr | Verifies that a list of facilities is formatted as a list of strings.
GIVEN two facilities with different IDs, names, and abbreviations.
WHEN facilitiesToStr is called.
THEN the returned list contains the formatted string for each facility in the original order.

Scenario: briefsToStr | Verifies that a list of briefs is formatted as a list of strings.
GIVEN two briefs with different IDs, mission IDs, titles, dates, and content.
WHEN briefsToStr is called.
THEN the returned list contains the formatted string for each brief in the original order.

Scenario: agentsToStr | Verifies that a list of agents is formatted as a list of strings.
GIVEN two agents with different IDs, facility IDs, names, birth dates, null death dates, and notes.
WHEN agentsToStr is called.
THEN the returned list contains the formatted string for each agent in the original order.

Scenario: usersToStr | Verifies that a list of users is formatted as a list of strings.
GIVEN two users with different IDs and usernames.
WHEN usersToStr is called.
THEN the returned list contains the formatted string for each user in the original order.

Scenario: logsToStr | Verifies that a list of logged actions is formatted as a list of strings.
GIVEN two logged actions associated with different users, dates, and records.
WHEN logsToStr is called.
THEN the returned list contains the formatted string for each logged action in the original order.

Scenario: messagesToStr | Verifies that a list of messages is formatted as a list of strings.
GIVEN two messages addressed to different agents with different message content.
WHEN messagesToStr is called.
THEN the returned list contains the formatted string for each message in the original order.